Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 17 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS by incisional biopsy  Extensive mammographically                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  EXTENSIVE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  FEW SCATTERED CELLS  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   DERMAL NEVUS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain a sufficient number of tumor cells to permit interpretation  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple aerolar complex and a 0 8cm in greatest dimension flesh colored papule located 2 0cm from the lateral side margin  Also present is a 2 0cm linear  well healed scar along the lateral side margin  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked in black while the anterior aspect of the specimen is inked in blue  Sectioning reveals predominantly fibrous parenchyma with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity underlying the skin scar and located 0 5cm from the nearest  deep  margin  Scattered throughout the fibrous parenchyma are multiple foci of gritty  firm  clusters of punctate  tan white to brown areas ranging in size from 0 4cm to 1 5cm and located up to 0 3cm from the deep margin and abutting the anterior margin  The biopsy cavity is submitted entirely in cassettes A through C medial to lateral with closest margin and skin papule in B  Representative sections of the gritty areas are submitted in cassettes D through G with closest deep margin in E and closest anterior margin in G  The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic changes and representative sections have been submitted in H and I  Labeled  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node bivalved and entirely submitted in J  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D            