 progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a simple mastectomy specimen  with skin ellipse measuring 5 x 2 5cm and a grossly unremarkable nipple  The breast itself measures 8 x 4 x 5cm  Sectioning reveals a stellate  ill defined lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is firm and more than 2cm from the closest inked margins  SECTION CODE A D  Stellate lesion submitted in toto  E G  Representative sections of breast parenchyma  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY , Negative.
