Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram left breast  Two lesions are noted in A and B                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  A   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    GRADE REMOVED_DATE EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Several microcalcifications are seen in slide A and E  No lymphatic or vascular invasion identifed  This tumor measures 1 1cm in diameter  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  B   INFILTRATING  80   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20    GRADE REMOVED_DATE EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Microcalcifications are seen in slide M  No lymphatic or vascular invascular invasion  The tumor measures 0 8cm in diameter  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  BOTH SPECIMENS   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  A  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibronodular fibrous tissue with localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate firm white lesion with central hemorrhagic focus measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm extending to the inked margin  Specimen is submitted in cassettes A through F  nodule in A   C  representative sections in cassettes D  E  and F  Representative section of nodule frozen and saved  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  B  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fatty fibrous tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  white nodule   1  approximately 1cm from inked margin  and a separate irregular white lesion   2  measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm at the margin  Nodule in cassette G  second irregular lesion  2 in cassettes H and I  Representative sections in J through N  Representative section of rounded nodule  1 saved frozen  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN A   SMALL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN B   SMALL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koern