Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 02 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  4 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 1   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLARY  LEVEL 2    TUMOR EMBOLI IN PERINODAL LYMPHATICS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLA  HOT SPOT  1  CT  90    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor penetrates the capsule of one lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate containers  Labeled  right breast and right axillary contents  lymphadenectomy Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm overlying skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm inverted nipple  centered on a 2 0cm in diameter ill defined areola  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm white to focally yellow granular stellate mass that extends to within 2 5cm of the closest inked resection margin  Anteriorly the mass extends to reach the overlying skin in the nipple area  focally showing paste like consistency  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  AandB  tumor and closest resection margin C F  tumor G I  unremarkable breast parenchyma J N  representative lymph nodes  Labeled  right axillary lymphadenectomy Level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  represenative lymmph nodes submitted in O and P  Labeled  right axilla  Hot spot  1  Ct 90  is an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  A representative lymph node is submitted in cassette Q  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  LEVEL 2 PART C  RIGHT AXILARY LYMP