area located 2 1cm of the posterior and 1 0cm of the anterior margin  Surrounding the area is dense  gray white fibrous tissue with two surrounding silver metal clips  Located 0 1cm anterior to the indurated area of second  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  gray white nodule  The suspicious indurated areas are located in the 12 00 region of the specimen and the surrounding dense gray white fibrous tissue is diffusely nodular with a vague stellate pattern  possibly consistent with previous biopsy site  The remaining mammary tissue shows diffuse  dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue  Sectioning of the axillary region reveals two possible tan red lymph nodes  measuring 0 5cm each  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Dense fibrous tissue surrounding suspicious indurated areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Indurated area  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule anterior to indurated area and representative adjacent dense fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Dense gray white fibrous tissue  lateral to indurated area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative fibrous tissue from lateral breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a black stitch designating the axilla  The specimen is partially surface by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm portion of unremarkable tan pink skin including a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm unremarkable tan pink nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal nodularity in the upper and lower outer quadrant  No discrete lesions or other abnormalities are identified  Representative sectioning of the axillary region reveals possible tan red lymph nodes  ranging from