t he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  received with a needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is received with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect of the specimen  as per the surgeon  There is an irregular  hemorrhagic  ragged area on the anterior surface  REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Superior   green  inferior   yellow  anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm firm  focally hemorrhagic  gray white area with ill defined borders focally abutting the anterior margin  0 4cm from the superior margin  0 9cm from the inferior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin  0 9cm from the lateral margin  and 1 0cm from the medial margin  The remaining cut surfaces consist of yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue  with no additional lesions grossly appreciated  The specimen is submitted in toto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   sequentially from lateral to medial  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body  submitted sequentially from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as 