Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 MAY 02 ACCESSIONED ON  29 MAY 02 at 12 53 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old white female  status post stereotactic core biopsy of a lobulated mass in the inferio medial left breast   carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 05                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block E  Core Biopsy  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast   are multiple tan cylindrical soft tissues ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm which are submitted in toto as A E  Gross Description by  LAURA NAKATSUKA Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Elizabeth Miller  M D  Eren D Yeh  M D  Helenanne D al