gy Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node   are 2 pieces of fibroadipose tissue and lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The larger portion of tissue is bisected and is submitted entirely as frozen section  1  the smaller of the two lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely as frozen section  2  Frozen section  1 is now resubmitted as A  and  2 as B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE fragment of breast tissue with a short stitch demarcating the superior margin and a long stitch demarcating the lateral margin  The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity  which lies 0 5cm from the closest  mid posterior  margin  There are surrounding tan white fibrous tissue around the biopsy cavity along with an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregular shaped tan white gritty region  which is approximately 1 6cm from the closest  mid posterior  margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  C E  biopsy cavity and adjacent mid posterior margin  entirely submitted  F  adjacent nodule and adjacent closest margin  G  medial edge of smaller nodule  H  lateral extent of breast specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and u