Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  ASSOCIATED WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIUM DEPOSITION  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma measures 1 5cm from the glass slide  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is noted  Hormone analysis studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a