ptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 12 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fibrofatty fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nodule  No frozen section done  The fragment is submitted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE  AandB  nodule CandD  regions flanking the nodule E M  unremarkable tissue  Enclosed is the lesions radiograph  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  SAVED FOR PERMANENT SECTION  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
