Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is noted  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen recptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone protien  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  only is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm excision specimen with localizing wire in place  Inked and stained to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm stellate nodule which abuts the inked resection margin in multiple locations  Submitted entirely in A through E  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
